{
  "journal": [
    {
      "at": 360,
      "text": "You swim until your arms stop answering. Then sand scrapes your knees. You crawl out of the surf and lie still, the knife in your hand.",
      "turn": 7,
    },
    {
      "at": 360,
      "text": "You come to at the tide line, clothes heavy with water. Nothing on the horizon, nothing left of the ship. Behind the dunes, trees.",
      "turn": 9,
    },
    {
      "at": 390,
      "text": "From the crest of the dunes you see the island's edge give way to trees. A forest, an hour's walk at most.",
      "turn": 12,
    },
    {
      "at": 390,
      "text": "You could reach the forest from here.",
      "turn": 13,
    },
    {
      "at": 420,
      "text": "At the far end of the beach, a ring of rocks breaks the sea wind. It is a natural shelter. You can make a bed here, and build a campfire for warmth.",
      "turn": 17,
    },
    {
      "at": 450,
      "text": "Past the rocks, a low cliff drops into the surf. Shells cling to the wet stone below it. You could pick them and eat them as they are. Cooked, they would go further.",
      "turn": 22,
    },
    {
      "at": 450,
      "text": "You gather stones where the cliff has crumbled.",
      "turn": 25,
    },
    {
